  "body": "**What happens.** The rapid law in `crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs` (about line 112) acquits each vertical rapid that moves up. It judges only a vertical rapid that moves down, against the stock column. An upward retract that crosses the part (for example a ledge or a canopy above the tool) gets no warning.\n\nThe envelope scan also omits rapid moves (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan.rs`, about line 325). Thus no verify pass convicts such a retract.\n\n**Where it came from.** The SAFETY review of PR #4050 (issue #3330) found this gap. The multi-axis contour now refuses a blocked plunge or retract column at its picks. The automatic paths of other operations still depend on the verify pass as their guard.\n\n**Expected.** Each vertical rapid, up or down, is checked against the part with the tool's swept volume (ball or shank as applicable). A rapid that touches the part gives a warning that blocks the post (AGENTS.md Prime Directive).\n\n**Note on priority.** The generators that emit such a retract refuse it at generation where a pick law exists. This issue is the verify backstop, thus P3.\n\nDone means:\n- An upward vertical rapid that crosses part material gives a named warning in the verify pass.\n- A pin in the sim suites shows a retract under a canopy convicted, and a retract in open air acquitted.\n",
